//// Design §5(a), front 17 step 4 — a `PersistentTerm` var is written once, at
//// load: every `persistent_term:put` scans every process heap, and `-on_load`
//// re-runs on every code reload, so a value written at run time is erased by
//// the next one (`999` → `101`, measured). Refused at the assignment, on every
//// target — the annotation's contract does not depend on where it runs.

#[@BeamMemory.PersistentTerm]
var version: i32 = 101;

pub fn main() {
    version = 102;
    @print(version);
}
